SUMMARY:[Council Meeting · Kelowna] Kelowna City Council: First Regular Me
 eting of New Term
DESCRIPTION:WHEN: Monday\, November 9\, 2026\, 1:30 p.m. to 5:00 p.m. (Kelo
 wna time)\nWHERE: Council Chamber\, Kelowna City Hall\, 1435 Water Street\
 , Kelowna\, BC\n\nCATEGORY: Municipal Government\nTYPE: Council Meeting\nJ
 URISDICTION: Kelowna\nFEDERAL RIDING: Kelowna\nTAGS: Open to Public\, Free
 \, Livestreamed\, Mayor & Council\n\nABOUT:\nFirst regular meeting of the 
 2026–2030 council. Kelowna's regular public meetings are Mondays at 1:30
  p.m.\; council also meets Monday mornings at 9 a.m. for policy and in-cam
 era business. Livestreamed at kelowna.ca/council. Check the agenda for the
  exact times.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS (GOVERNMENT RELATIONS):\nThe first busines
 s meeting of the new council signals early priorities and which staff repo
 rts come forward first.\n\nDETAILS:\nOrganizer: City of Kelowna\nWho atten
 ds: Mayor and council\, City senior staff\, delegations\nCost: Free\nAcces
 s: Open to the public\nLivestream: Livestreamed and archived at kelowna.ca
 /council\nAgenda: Posted at kelowna.ca/council\n\nNOT YET CONFIRMED: Exact
  afternoon start time\; check the agenda.\n\nSOURCE: https://www.am1150.ca
 /90986/news/municipal-news/city-of-kelowna/new-kelowna-city-council-to-be-
 sworn-in/
LOCATION:Council Chamber\, Kelowna City Hall\, 1435 Water Street\, Kelowna\
 , BC
CATEGORIES:Municipal Government,Council Meeting,Kelowna,Open to Public,Free
 ,Livestreamed,Mayor & Council
