  Kelowna Innovation Centre (Theatre)\, 460 Doyle Avenue\, Kelowna\, BC\n\n
 CATEGORY: Business & Economic Policy\nTYPE: Policy Briefing\nJURISDICTION:
  Kelowna\nFEDERAL RIDING: Kelowna\nTAGS: Registration Required\, Senior Pu
 blic Servants\, Business Leaders\, Trade & Economy\, Networking Opportunit
 y\, GR Must-Attend\, Details TBC\n\nABOUT:\nA three-hour in-person session
  led by Sara Wilshaw\, Canada's Chief Trade Commissioner\, with the Kelown
 a Chamber\, on diversifying into EU and Indo-Pacific markets. Highly relev
 ant to federal trade policy and government relations. Start time not publi
 shed (time TBC). Registration has closed (Chamber deadline Nov 3)\; Chambe
 r event page: https://secure.kelownachamber.org/events/TradeDiversificatio
 n%20Where%20Do%20We%20Stand-7843/details\n\nWHY IT MATTERS (GOVERNMENT REL
 ATIONS):\nRare local access to one of Canada's most senior trade officials
 \; directly relevant to federal trade policy and Canada–US trade.\n\nDET
 AILS:\nOrganizer: Kelowna Chamber of Commerce with the Trade Commissioner 
 Service (Global Affairs Canada)\nWho attends: Sara Wilshaw (Chief Trade Co
 mmissioner of Canada)\, exporters\, Chamber members\nAccess: Registration 
 required\; registration has closed\nRegistration / tickets: https://secure
 .kelownachamber.org/events/TradeDiversification%20Where%20Do%20We%20Stand-
 7843/details\n\nNOT YET CONFIRMED: Start time not published.\n\nSOURCE: ht
 tps://www.tradecommissioner.gc.ca/en/trade-events-training/2026/11/trade-d
 iversification-where-do-we-stand.html
LOCATION:Kelowna Innovation Centre (Theatre)\, 460 Doyle Avenue\, Kelowna\,
  BC
